course: dictionary
lesson: 161
title: Words that tell us when
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Afterwards» is an adverb that means later, after something else has happened. It tells us when something happens compared with something else. «Let's tidy up first and play afterwards» means the tidying comes before the playing.
explain: Writers use «afterwards» as a time connective to put events in order: first, then, next, afterwards, finally. Look at the words around it for clues. In «Sam spoke up in assembly, and afterwards the class looked at him differently», the word tells us the looking came after the speaking.
explain: Numbers work the same way. «She had 12 sweets. Afterwards she ate 5» means she started with 12 and then took away 5, so the sum is 12 − 5. To check your meaning, swap in «later»: if the sentence still makes sense, you have it right.
fact: Afterwards means later, after something else has happened.
fact: «Afterwards» is an adverb: it tells us when something happens.
fact: «Soon afterwards», «shortly afterwards» and «straight afterwards» all mean a short time later, and «long afterwards» means a long time later.
fact: «A loot box is a paid mystery prize in a game: you pay, it opens, and you only find out afterwards what you got.» Here it means you learn the prize after you have paid.
fact: «Afterwards the body remembers that germ and beats it quickly next time.» Here it means after the first meeting with the germ, not before it.
exercise: «Let's tidy up first and play afterwards.» What does afterwards mean here? | *Later, after tidying up | Before tidying up | At the same time as tidying up | Never
exercise: «She had 12 sweets. Afterwards she ate 5.» Which sum shows the second step? | *12 − 5 | 12 + 5 | 5 − 12 | 12 × 5
exercise: «Sam spoke up in assembly, and afterwards the class looked at him differently.» Find and copy the word that shows the looking came later. | assembly | spoke | *afterwards | differently
test: Which phrase means a short time later? | Long before | Once upon a time | *Shortly afterwards | At the very start
test: Which word is a time connective used to put events in order? | Bigger | *Afterwards | Blue | Quickly
exam: Which sentence uses «afterwards» to mean later? | Afterwards is a long word. | I afterwards like pizza. | *We ate our lunch, and afterwards we went to the park. | The afterwards bus was red.
